{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"To factor means to rewrite an expression as a product. Let's try dividing the expression $60y-90-20x$ by each factor.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $5$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}60y-90-20x\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\left(\\dfrac{60y-90-20x}{5}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\left(\\dfrac{60y}{5}-\\dfrac{90}{5}-\\dfrac{20x}{5}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5(12y-18-4x)\n\\end{align}$\n\nWe see that $60y-90-20x$ is equivalent to $5(12y-18-4x)$, not to $5(14y-16-4x)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $2$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}60y-90-20x\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2\\left(\\dfrac{60y-90-20x}{2}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2\\left(\\dfrac{60y}{2}-\\dfrac{90}{2}-\\dfrac{20x}{2}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2(30y-45-10x)\n\\end{align}$\n\nNo, $60y-90-20x$ is *not* equivalent to $2(30-45-10)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $10$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}60y-90-20x\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=10\\left(\\dfrac{60y-90-20x}{10}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=10\\left(\\dfrac{60y}{10}-\\dfrac{90}{10}-\\dfrac{20x}{10}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=10(6y-9-2x)\n\\end{align}$\n\nYes, $60y-90-20x$ is equivalent to $10(6y-9-2x)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"The following expressions are equivalent to $60y-90-20x$:\n\n- $5(12y-18-4x)$\n- $10(6y-9-2x)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Factor $60y-90-20x$ to identify the equivalent expressions.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $70y-80-20x$.","content":"$5(14y-16-4x)$","correct":false},{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $60-90-20$.","content":"$2(30-45-10)$","correct":false},{"clue":"